From 6bb9473983365f301931d7cf5fa190f7094b503e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: czekoloczek <czekoloczek@pierdolnik.xyz>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 03:31:41 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] ARM64: dts: p3s: Drop the 96 Hz based display modes

The 96HS mode and the 48HS mode (96HS with a TE HW skip) switch the
panel's driving frequency from 120 Hz to 96 Hz, which shifts its gamma.
With adaptive refresh rate SurfaceFlinger idles from 120 Hz to 48 Hz and
back on every small update (a blinking cursor, a seconds clock), so the
screen visibly flickers in tone.

60 Hz is already 120HS with a TE HW skip, so 120 <-> 60 Hz keeps the
panel at 120 Hz and is invisible. Remove the 96 Hz based mode nodes for
all p3s board revisions, together with their exposed-mode entries,
__symbols__ entries and __local_fixups__ offsets. Dropping them from
exposed-mode alone is not enough: of_get_panel_display_modes() parses
every child node and nothing reads exposed-mode. SurfaceFlinger still
switches between 120 and 60 Hz, and LFD still lowers the panel refresh
rate on static content.

Same idea as exy2100 34237952a ("r9s: Fix adaptive refresh rate color
flickering").

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
